        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-13T01:38:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you mean the buffer of std::string that is allocated on heap? Yes, you can always explicitly zero it before destructing std::string. Or you might be able to use another API in libcutils [1] which uses user-provided buffer for storing the value of the prop.\n\nhttps://source.corp.google.com/android/system/core/libcutils/include/cutils/properties.h;rcl\u003d3431b4ee870dd270ac6327c42d298069de882b69;l\u003d49",
      "parentUuid": "faf89db1_644d3ce1",
      "range": {
